{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T21:07:13.136Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 is complete. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Implementation** (`src/cli/mcp.ts`): added `registerMcpCommand`, `runMcpServer`, and `serveMcpStdio`. It registers `osq mcp --cwd <dir>`, targets the project locally or the server when `OSQ_SERVER` is set, and serves the nine tools over stdio — one JSON-RPC message per line in, one JSON answer per line out through `processStdout` only. Non-JSON lines get the `-32700` parse error; `tools/call` chains one at a time while other messages answer immediately; stdin close drains every read request and exits 0.\n\n**Wiring**: registered the command in `index.ts` (moving `parseRejectReason` unchanged into `reject.ts` to stay at 244 lines), added `mcp` after `server` in the help group, and updated `tests/help-groups.test.ts` accordingly.\n\n**README**: added the command line and a \"Planning through MCP\" section before \"Running osq on a server\".\n\n**Tests**: added `tests/mcp-cli.test.ts`, spawning `bin.ts` through tsx with an empty `OSQ_SERVER` and a temp home, covering the pipelined planning session and the Not JSON line, killing every process in an `after` hook.\n\nVerification: task verify passes (2/2); `pnpm verify` passes end to end (typecheck, build, full suite, lint). Result written to `openspec/changes/163-local-mcp/.run/results/4.md`."}}
